  "i409": "{\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nSince #292, an elided `typescript` call and its result appear in the model's context as assistant text, for example:\\n\\n```\\n[Pit: elided tool call: typescript · ~739 tokens with its result · reason: absorbed into assistant replies and note state-2026-11-18 · originals: session.inspectEntry(\\\"3c47487c\\\"), session.inspectEntry(\\\"7ba62e94\\\")]\\n```\\n\\nIn a long session with many of these, the model started writing that same text itself at the end of a turn, where it meant to call the tool. The message then has **no tool call**, so nothing runs, but the transcript renders it exactly like an elided call. The model (and the person reading the transcript) took each one as a completed action. #292 fixed models copying the placeholder *as a tool argument*; this is the text form being copied instead, with a worse failure mode: no error, no retry, a silent no-op.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\nIn one session (pi 1.5.2, pit `git:github.com/cv/pit@main`, extension changelog 0.37.0, model `claude-opus-5-5` via `nvidia-internal/azure/anthropic`), it happened at least 4 times in the session file, plus more earlier that were only caught later:\\n\\n| Assistant entry | Time (UTC) | Tool calls in the message | What the model believed it did |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `e27e2e44` | 2026-11-18 06:45 | 0 | started two helper agents and closed a pull request |\\n| `e67f9b8a` | 2026-11-18 06:53 | 0 | started a read-only helper agent |\\n| `079f2e53` | 2026-11-18 10:19 | 0 | started a helper agent |\\n| `7e70ea50` | 2026-11-18 10:25\",\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"cv\",\"body\":\"@pi do you have enough information to reproduce this issue? and come up with a PR for a fix?\"},{\"author\":\"pi-action-agent\",\"body\":\"### 🤖 pi Response\\n\\nYes, the issue had enough detail to reproduce it, and the fix is up as PR [#410](https://github.com/cv/pit/pull/410). All local checks pass, including tests and coverage. CI fails on Node 22, but in the dependency audit step, not in this change; Node 24 and 26 were still running when I last checked.\\n\\n**Reproduction:** step 4 of the issue is the exact trigger. It's a finished assistant reply with no tool call whose last line starts with `[Pit: elided tool call`. Before the fix, Pit did nothing at the end of such a turn, so the run stopped with nothing executed and no notice. \"}],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Models imitate elided calls rendered as text: they write the placeholder instead of calling the tool, and nothing runs\"}\n",
  "i402": "{\"body\":\"@pi ship a patch release\",\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"pi-action-agent\",\"body\":\"### 🤖 pi Response\\n\\nv0.38.1 isn't shipped yet. The version bump is merged to `main`, but CI on that commit failed its dependency security check, so I didn't create the tag.\\n\\n**What's done**\\n- Release PR #403 (`chore(release): v0.38.1`): bumps `package.json` and `package-lock.json` to 0.38.1, adds a `## [0.38.1]` changelog entry and points the README's pinned install example at `@v0.38.1`.\\n- The release has one change since v0.38.0, commit `ac49133`: when a `typescript` call puts its label or options in a `// @pit: {...}` header, the call display now shows them.\\n- Local check, tests, coverage an\"}],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"new patch release\"}\n",
  "p410": "{\"body\":\"Refs #409. Not closing yet: this changes what the model and the transcript see, so it needs a live Pi check first.\\n\\n## Reproduction\\n\\nThe issue gives enough to reproduce this without the session file. Its step 4 test is the trigger: a completed assistant message whose last text line is an `[Pit: elided tool call…]` record and that has no `toolCall` block. Before this change, Pit's `turn_end` boundary returned nothing for such a message, so the run settled with no tool result and no notice. The new test `test/globals/imitated-calls.test.ts` builds that exact message on a real Pi `SessionManager`. A mutation probe that disables the notice makes its two positive tests fail (`expected undefined to be true`).\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- **Detect it and say so (proposal 1).** `src/context/imitated-calls.ts` flags a completed reply that makes no tool call and whose last line starts with the elided-call prefix. At `turn_end`, Pit appends a `pit.imitated-call` notice saying no tool ran and the action did not happen, and returns `continue: true` so the model gets one more response to make the call.\\n  - **Loop guard:** if the reply right after a notice repeats the mistake, it gets the notice again but no c\",\"closes\":[],\"title\":\"Notice replies that write an elided-call record instead of calling a tool (#409)\"}\n"
}
